{"body":"**System information**\r\n- TensorFlow.js version (you are using): 2.8.6\r\n- Are you willing to contribute it (Yes/No): Yes\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n**Describe the feature and the current behavior/state.**\r\nCurrently the [tf.node.encodeJpeg()](https://js.tensorflow.org/api_node/3.1.0/#node.encodeJpeg) method only accepts Uint8 Tensor3D as input. This is incovenient as many of the tensors generated by images or the [ react-native HOC](https://js.tensorflow.org/api_react_native/0.5.0/#cameraWithTensors) are in dtype: Int32. This makes converting generated tensors back to jpg/png difficult as there isn't any methods for converting Int32 to uint8.\r\n\r\n\r\n**Will this change the current api? How?**\r\nThis will allow additional input the the encodeJpeg method to allow a broader range of inputs. In addition, this will add more consistency as decodeJpeg() generates an Int32 tensor, but it can't be converted back to the original jpeg with encodeJpeg().\r\n\r\n**Who will benefit with this feature?**\r\nReact native users and other users who deal with Tensor3D in Int32 format.\r\n\r\n**Any Other info.**\r\nExample: Tensor3D generated from the [react-native HOC](https://js.tensorflow.org/api_react_native/0.5.0/#cameraWithTensors) , the dtype is Int32 and therefore the original image can't be accessed for OCR, image processing etc.\r\n<img width=\"234\" alt=\"Screen Shot 2021-02-22 at 5 57 38 PM\" src=\"https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/44853346/108781153-74e8d880-7537-11eb-919d-dfc35e982be9.png\">\r\n\r\n","canonical_uri":"https://github.com/tensorflow/tfjs/issues/4727","relation_events":[],"repository":"tensorflow/tfjs","updated_at":"2021-08-26T16:58:12Z"}